  "body": "https://matrix.org/docs/spec/client_server/latest#m-room-power-levels\r\n\r\n**Issue**\r\nThe default level for `invite` (if it is not specified) is given as 50.\r\n\r\n**Expected behaviour**\r\nAccording to Synapse it is 0 (see https://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/pull/10254#discussion_r662545610). Note that Synapse defaults *new rooms* to specify an invite level of 50, but when not given it should default to 0. @erikjohnston asserted the spec is incorrect and not Synapse.\r\n\r\nSee https://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/blob/2d16e69b4bf09b5274a8fa15c8ca4719db8366c1/synapse/event_auth.py#L177 (and other callers of `_get_named_level` with the invite level) which all specify as 0.\r\n\r\nIt looks like matrix-org/matrix-spec-proposals#341 added these defaults, the others are correct according to Synapse.\r\n",
